# Confluence create

## Gate

Ordinary coding stays **pageless**. Do not create a page, invent a space, or
open Confluence to “cover” work unless this turn explicitly authorizes it.

Create **only** when the user text clearly says to file one, for example:

- “make a Confluence page”, “document this in Confluence”, “write a wiki
  page”, “create a page in …”

These do **not** authorize create — just implement on the current branch:

- “add X”, “fix Y”, “I think Z is broken”, naming a feature without docs

Naming an **existing** page (id, or title + space) means update or read that
page — it does not mean create another one. Follow `confluence-update`.

Ambiguity → **do not create**. Never ask whether to file a page unless the
user already raised docs filing.

## Create-only is the default

“Make a Confluence page / document this” authorizes **create only**. Put the
rest of the message into the page body (see `confluence-structure`) and
**stop**. Do not edit product code, open a worktree, or invent follow-up
tickets.

`global-execute-first` does **not** override create-only when the primary
verb this turn is docs/wiki/Confluence create.

## Create-and-implement (explicit second verb only)

Same-turn product implementation only when the user adds an explicit second
verb, for example: “document it and implement it”, “create the page and build
it”. Inference (“they described the work, so build it”) is forbidden.

## Defaults (never invent)

When create is authorized:

1. **Space** — host-configured default when present; else a space the
   operator or chat already named. Never invent a space key.
2. **Parent page** — user-named parent wins; else host-configured default
   parent when set; else space root only when that is clearly intended. Do
   not invent a parent title or id.
3. **Template** — use only when the user names a template or host config
   requires one. Prefer `confluence_create_page_from_template` then, else
   plain `confluence_create_page`.

Prefer a connected Confluence / Atlassian MCP when ready (`global-mcp-first`).
Do not invent credentials or side CLIs while MCP works.

## Search before create

Before minting a new page:

1. `confluence_search` (or space tree) for the intended title / topic in the
   resolved space.
2. If a near-duplicate exists, **update that page** (`confluence-update`)
   unless the user explicitly wants a second page.
3. Only create when no reasonable match exists.

## Types

| Type | Default create? | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Page | Yes | `confluence-page` |
| Blog post | Only if user asks for a blog | lighter Overview body; still no invent space |
| Folder / parent shell | Only if user asks for a container | Overview + children links later |

## Create procedure

1. Resolve space / parent / template from host config or explicit context —
   never invent.
2. Search for duplicates in that space.
3. Apply `confluence-structure` + `confluence-page`.
4. Create via MCP (or host-approved CLI if no MCP).
5. Diagrams when the user asked for figures: `confluence-diagrams`.
6. Return the page title, id, and browse link when the site URL is known.
